        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karla Bonoff, Bonnie Raitt, Wynonna Judd, Lynn Anderson, Naomi Judd\n- Roles: songwriter, singer/songwriter\n- Music Works: \"Home,\" \"Tell Me Why,\" \"Isn't It Always Love,\" Wild Heart of the Young\n- Groups: The Judds\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1980s, Wynonna Judd first rose to fame alongside her mother Naomi in the country music duo The Judds.\n- Wild Heart of the Young is the third album by singer/songwriter Karla Bonoff.\n- As a songwriter, Karla Bonoff had songs interpreted by other artists, including Bonnie Raitt recording \"Home,\" Wynonna Judd recording \"Tell Me Why,\" and Lynn Anderson recording \"Isn't It Always Love.\"",
